<%# locals: (event:) %>
<%#
  Every tag the tally carries, in the order it carries them, so the counted statuses stay the
  model's business alone. `invited` is the one whose label is not its own name: the legend calls
  that tally "no reply".

  An event nobody has been asked about sums to zero, because `reserved` is the one status
  `Event#answer_counts` leaves out, and says so in words instead: a card drawing nothing there
  reads as a card that failed to load the answers rather than as one with no answers to show. An
  event with no registrations at all still draws nothing, since "0 on the list" is not a fact
  worth a line.
%>
<% counts = event.answer_counts %>
<% if counts.values.any?(&:positive?) %>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
    <% counts.each do |status, count| %>
      <span class="badge badge-sm gap-1">
        <%= icon status, label: (status == "invited" ? "no reply" : status), class: "size-3.5" %>
        <%= count %>
      </span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% elsif (waiting = event.registrations.size).positive? %>
  <p class="text-card-fact">Nobody asked yet · <%= waiting %> on the list</p>
<% end %>
